[56db77c02ec04d1f] (mini.proposal.v1)
I expect the kernel 'conformance.kernel.recovery' to move from the original JSON object to 'NO_OBJECT' (or a different object) when the input is a strict JSON object and the transform 'conformance.transform.upper-case' is applied. According to the registry, this kernel tracks the object the harness recovers as canonical JSON. Since JSON keys and string values are case-sensitive and the structural characters (like braces) are not affected by upper-casing, but the content is, transforming a valid JSON object to all capitals will likely result in an invalid JSON structure or a different object if the harness cannot parse the upper-cased keys/values as the original. The catalogue already shows that 'conformance.kernel.recovery' moves under 'conformance.transform.upper-case' for a specific input, confirming this behavior.
commitments: {"input": "{}", "kernel": "conformance.kernel.recovery", "transform": "conformance.transform.upper-case"}
